{"name":"Chestnut","hex":"#742802","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Chestnut","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Chestnut"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chestnut","blocks":[{"text":"Chestnuts are the deciduous trees and shrubs in the genus Castanea, in the beech family Fagaceae. The name also refers to the edible nuts they produce. They are native to temperate regions of the Northern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Ch%C3%A2taignier_120807_1.jpg/330px-Ch%C3%A2taignier_120807_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chestnut"},{"title":"Chestnut (horse color)","blocks":[{"text":"Chestnut is a hair coat color of horses consisting of a reddish-to-brown coat with a mane and tail the same or lighter in color than the coat. Chestnut is characterized by the absolute absence of true black hairs. It is one of the most common horse coat colors, seen in almost every breed of horse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Pottok.jpg/330px-Pottok.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chestnut_(horse_color)"},{"title":"Chestnut (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Chestnut or castaneous is a colour, a medium reddish shade of brown, and is named after the nut of the chestnut tree. An alternate name for the colour is badious."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chestnut_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG/500px-Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG/1280px-Chestnuts_at_Ljubljana_Central_Market.JPG?utm_source=e